---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/v2/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterBlock from '../../../components/v2/NewsletterBlock.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';

const sections = [
  {
    title: 'The Peninsula road structure',
    body: [
      'The Mornington Peninsula Freeway (M11) is the spine. It runs south from Melbourne to Rosebud, with exits to every major town along Port Phillip Bay.',
      'Point Nepean Road runs along the bay from Mornington to Portsea — the old coastal road, slower but more scenic. Use it for short hops between bay-side towns; use the freeway for longer jumps.',
      'For Red Hill, Main Ridge, Merricks and the hinterland, the main arterial is Arthurs Seat Road (up from Dromana) and then a series of scenic connecting roads through the plateau. The roads are narrow, winding and full of cellar-door traffic on weekends.',
      'For Cape Schanck and the southern tip, Boneo Road and Cape Schanck Road are the routes. Expect slower going on summer weekends.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Parking',
    body: [
      'Most Peninsula towns have free on-street parking outside peak season. Summer Saturdays in Sorrento, Mornington and Portsea are the exception — arrive early (before 10am) or late (after 3pm).',
      'Parks Victoria charges a day-parking fee at some Mornington Peninsula National Park carparks (Cape Schanck, Point Nepean). Check the Parks Victoria site for current rates.',
      'Cellar doors and wineries provide their own parking; usually free for guests with a booking or buying.',
      'Beach carparks — most are free. Sorrento Back Beach and Portsea Back Beach fill by 10am in summer; arrive early.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Scenic drives',
    body: [
      'Arthurs Seat Road from Dromana up to the summit — the classic Peninsula ascent. Panoramic view at the top. Drive up, park briefly, walk the summit circuit.',
      'The Red Hill plateau loop — Mornington-Flinders Road through Red Hill, down Shoreham Road, along the southern coast via Flinders to Cape Schanck and back north via Rosebud. 90 minutes of driving, half a day with stops.',
      'Point Nepean Road from Mornington to Portsea — the old coastal route with bay views. Slow, pretty, best mid-morning or late afternoon.',
      'The Western Port side — Stony Point, Crib Point, Flinders. Quieter than the Port Phillip side, different character. Good for a less-travelled Peninsula morning.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Cycling',
    body: [
      'The Bay Trail — shared path along Port Phillip Bay from Mount Martha to Rosebud. Flat, family-friendly, 20+ km. Hire e-bikes in Mornington if you don\'t have your own.',
      'Red Hill cellar-door circuit — the plateau is rideable but the roads are narrow and traffic is real. Cycle it on weekday mornings, not summer weekends.',
      'Peninsula Hot Springs to Cape Schanck — the back roads are scenic but not purpose-built for cycling. Take care.',
      'Most Peninsula towns have bike racks; few have dedicated bike lanes outside the Bay Trail.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Ferry',
    body: [
      'The Sorrento–Queenscliff ferry is the most useful non-driving connection. 40 minutes across Port Phillip Bay, every hour. Takes cars, bikes, and foot passengers.',
      'Useful for three reasons: combining Peninsula with the Bellarine or Great Ocean Road; avoiding the Melbourne drive loop; and as a scenic experience on its own.',
      'The Stony Point to Phillip Island ferry is a useful connection for the eastern side — pedestrian only, useful if you\'re touring without a car.',
      'Book the car ferry ahead in peak season; walk-up tickets are available but spaces fill.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Rideshare',
    body: [
      'Uber and DiDi operate on the Peninsula but coverage is inconsistent, especially at night and in the hinterland. Taxis are almost non-existent outside central Mornington.',
      'Pre-booked winery tour drivers are the Peninsula-specific solution for a cellar-door afternoon. Multiple operators. Book ahead; expect $400–800 for half-day private charter.',
      'Hotel concierges can arrange drivers for longer-distance transfers. Useful when driving yourself after a long lunch is not sensible.',
      'For a full wine-tasting day, assume you will need a driver. Tasting responsibly and driving are in tension; the answer is a pre-booked driver.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting Around the Mornington Peninsula — Peninsula Insider"
  description="How to move around the Peninsula — roads, parking, scenic drives, cycling, ferry and rideshare. Practical intelligence for planning a trip that actually flows."
  section="explore"
  ogImage="/images/sourced/explore-hub-hero-01.webp"
>

  <section class="hero" aria-label="Getting around cover">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__frame">
        <div class="hero__above">
          <div class="hero__meta">
            <a href={`${base}explore/`} class="hero__meta-tag" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Explore</a>
            <span class="hero__meta-divider"></span>
            <span class="hero__meta-date">Practical transport</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="hero__headline">Moving around the Peninsula.</h1>
          <p class="hero__dek">The Peninsula is genuinely hard to navigate without a car. These are the roads, routes, parking realities and alternatives that actually work — and when rideshare or the ferry makes more sense than driving.</p>
        </div>
        <figure>
          <img class="hero__image" src={`${base}images/sourced/explore-hub-hero-01.webp`} alt="Peninsula roads" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
          <figcaption class="hero__image-cap">
            <span>Peninsula hinterland</span>
            <span>Photography <span class="ornament">/</span> The Insider</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {sections.map(s => (
    <section class="letter">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="letter__frame" style="display:block;">
          <div class="letter__eyebrow">
            <span class="letter__eyebrow-rule"></span>
            <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--ochre">{s.title}</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="letter__head">{s.title}.</h2>
          <div class="letter__prose">
            {s.body.map(p => <p>{p}</p>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <NewsletterBlock />

</BaseLayout>
